    "1": {
      "note": "Normal leaf stages start individually: Worker at build, Reviewer at freeze and Curator after code PASS; required notices reach Manager before direct peer handovers. Messaging resolves one live seat or refuses ambiguity. Further messages are held behind already waiting work; unfinished starts, pending permission and turns whose providers do not take steering postpone delivery without answering the permission. The product’s active sweep or ended-turn drain delivers admissible held work without sender resubmission. CODE and MEMORY keep separate recorded counts under the settings limit and recorded extra-round authority. Manager retains gate and transaction ownership and relays no peer contents.",
